stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB

  [*] --> ShellRequested

  state "Shell requested" as ShellRequested
  state "WASM boot mask" as Booting
  state "Anonymous" as Anon
  state "Authenticated" as Authed
  state "Access denied" as Denied

  ShellRequested --> Booting : MapRazorComponents(App)<br/>.AllowAnonymous()

  state Booting {
    direction TB
    [*] --> Framework
    Framework : /_framework/* forced AllowAnonymous
    Framework : (else fallback policy 302s the boot<br/>manifest and the app never boots)
    Framework --> Hydrate
    Hydrate : AddAuthenticationStateSerialization →<br/>AddAuthenticationStateDeserialization
    Hydrate : claims only, never tokens
    Hydrate --> [*]
  }

  Booting --> Anon : no auth cookie
  Booting --> Authed : cookie valid,<br/>principal deserialized

  state "Engine selection (startup)" as Engine
  [*] --> Engine
  Engine : Auth:EnableFakeAuth &amp;&amp; !Production → FakeAuthHandler
  Engine : AzureAd:ClientId set → Cookie + OpenIdConnect
  Engine : otherwise (non-prod) → Cookie only
  Engine : Production without ClientId → throws at startup

  Anon --> Challenging : navigate to [Authorize] page<br/>or GET /challenge-microsoft
  state "Challenging" as Challenging
  Challenging --> Authed : OIDC code flow →<br/>/signin-oidc → cookie issued
  Challenging --> Anon : user cancels

  Anon --> Authed : GET /auth/login/fake<br/>(Dev GUEST only)
  Anon --> Anon : /api/* → 401 (never a 302)

  Authed --> Denied : /api/diag in Production and<br/>email not in Diagnostics:AdminEmails
  Denied --> Authed : allow-list updated
  Authed --> Anon : GET /auth/logout<br/>cookie + OIDC sign-out
  Authed --> Anon : cookie expires
